ParsingUtils: TokenMatchI must not step past the buffer terminator

Backport of upstream assimp commit 23fac9e7 ("don't step past the terminator in
TokenMatchI", PR #6737) -- merged after our pinned release tag v6.0.5.

The bug
-------
    if (!ASSIMP_strincmp(token, in, len) && IsSpaceOrNewLine(in[len])) {
        in += len + 1;

`IsSpaceOrNewLine` is true for '\0', so a token sitting at the very end of the
buffer matched and then advanced the cursor ONE PAST the terminator -- the
parser then reads whatever follows the allocation. TokenMatchI is used by the
text importers we compile (OBJ/MTL and Collada-adjacent parsing helpers) on
file content.

The fix
-------
Advance past the delimiter only when there is a delimiter; otherwise stop on
the terminator.

Documented deviation from upstream: the test/unit/Common/utParsingUtils.cpp
hunk is dropped (ASSIMP_BUILD_TESTS is OFF in irisgl/CMakeLists.txt, so assimp's
own test tree is never compiled). Our coverage for this class of fix is
tests/importer.

diff --git a/include/assimp/ParsingUtils.h b/include/assimp/ParsingUtils.h
--- a/include/assimp/ParsingUtils.h
+++ b/include/assimp/ParsingUtils.h
@@ -257,7 +257,12 @@ AI_FORCE_INLINE bool TokenMatch(char_t *&in, const char *token, unsigned int len
 /// @return true if token was found, false if not.
 AI_FORCE_INLINE bool TokenMatchI(const char *&in, const char *token, unsigned int len) {
     if (!ASSIMP_strincmp(token, in, len) && IsSpaceOrNewLine(in[len])) {
-        in += len + 1;
+        if (in[len] != '\0') {
+            in += len + 1;
+        } else {
+            // If EOF after the token make sure we don't go past end of buffer
+            in += len;
+        }
         return true;
     }
     return false;
